	(text
		"DESIGN NOTES\n!! MAINS on the triac (Q1) and the MOC3063 output pins 4/6. The opto is the isolation barrier. !!\nMCU PB0/MOSI -> R1 (330R) -> MOC3063 LED (pins 1/2, SELV). Opto output (4/6) drives the BTA16 gate.\nMOC3063 is ZERO-CROSSING: it only fires near the mains zero-crossing -> low EMI, low gate inrush.\nRG1 180R = gate resistor (ACL_F -> opto -> gate). RS1 100R + CS1 10 nF = dv/dt snubber across MT1-MT2.\nQ1 BTA16-600B: MT1(A1)=Line (ACL_F), MT2(A2)=Lamp. Derate / heatsink for lamp currents > ~2 A.\nVERIFY per ON AN-3004: peak opto current < 1 A ITSM; 180R OK for a zero-cross opto, raise to 360R if not."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c3b7223d-c0f0-524b-945a-4aec3a4c0cc5")
	)
	(text
		"PART NOTES (VERIFY = check against vendor datasheet before release)\nU2: Input LED (1,2) = SELV side; output triac (4,6) = mains side. Pins 3,5 NC. 8 mm land spacing keeps the opto's own primary-secondary PCB creepage >= 6 mm.\nR1: Opto LED current = (5 - 1.2 V)/330 ~ 11.5 mA > IFT(10 mA) of MOC3063. Driven by MCU PB0/MOSI.\nRG1: 180 ohm per the brief; ON AN-3004 suggests >=360 ohm for 230 V non-ZC - OK here because MOC3063 is zero-crossing (fires near 0 V). VERIFY peak opto current < ITSM(1 A).\nQ1: Non-snubberless part -> external snubber fitted (RS1/CS1). Derate: ~6 A continuous no heatsink. VERIFY heatsinking / lamp current; add a clip-on sink for >2 A loads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 219.71 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "62c36151-d3d9-5257-a930-82b53de726b9")
	)
)
